    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0175" n="73" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg73"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">719.2115/7</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting President of Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Porras</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July 23,
                            1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received August
                        11.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Phillips</hi>: As the Colombian Treaty
                    seems to have been definitely drafted and is now before the Senate waiting for
                    its ratification, the Government and people of Panama are concerned <pb
                        facs="0176" n="74" xml:id="pg74"/> about the provisions of that document,
                    specially as in all probability mention will be made in it of the boundary line
                    between Panama and Colombia.</p>
                <p>Owing to that circumstance I feel it my duty to inform the Government of the
                    United States through you, that Panama is in a position to prove her rights to a
                    boundary line that will follow the Atrato river from its mouth in the Atlantic
                    ocean to a point in the hinterland in a straight line with Cape Corrientes in
                    the Pacific ocean. That line will comprise within the borders of Panamá a region
                    pointed out as a possible competitor of the Canal Zone, as it affords a suitable
                    route for another interoceanic canal.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Belisario Porras</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
